      "leanVersion": "v4.33.0",
      "mathlibVersion": "db584cd6d46c92f209a44c0f1c829460d327499d",
      "title": "The Strong Nemhauser–Trotter Theorem for Vertex Cover",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Édouard Bonnet",
          "github": "EdouardBonnet"
        },
        {
          "name": "Codex"
        }
      ],
      "bibEntries": [
        "@inproceedings{ChlebikChlebikova2004,\n  author = {Miroslav Chlebík and Janka Chlebíková},\n  title = {Improvement of Nemhauser--Trotter Theorem and Its Applications in Parametrized Complexity},\n  booktitle = {Algorithm Theory -- SWAT 2004}, series = {LNCS},\n  volume = {3111}, pages = {174--186}, year = {2004},\n  doi = {10.1007/978-3-540-27810-8_16}\n}\n",
        "@article{NemhauserTrotter1974,\n  author = {Nemhauser, George L. and Trotter, Jr., Leslie E.},\n  title = {Properties of Vertex Packing and Independence System Polyhedra},\n  journal = {Mathematical Programming}, volume = {6},\n  pages = {48--61}, year = {1974}, doi = {10.1007/BF01580222}\n}\n"
      ]
    },
    "abstract": "Given a finite simple graph $G$, one polynomial-time word-RAM algorithm partitions its vertices into $V_0$, $V_{1/2}$, and $V_1$. Every neighbor of $V_0$ lies in $V_1$. Every vertex cover of $G[V_{1/2}]$ has size at least $|V_{1/2}|/2$. Every minimum vertex cover of $G$ contains $V_1$ and avoids $V_0$.\n\nChlebík and Chlebíková strengthened the Nemhauser–Trotter theorem to obtain the guarantee for every minimum vertex cover. The algorithm maximizes $|A|-|B|$ subject to $N(A)\\subseteq B$, breaking ties by minimizing $|A|$. A single rational linear program finds such a pair. The RAM reads the adjacency matrix and writes one label per vertex.\n"
  },
